      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOSH ALMIGHTY (10) brings the most appealing recent profile after closing strongly for second in a provincial CL1 at Kembla Grange, beaten a length after being well back and finding some trouble. Now back to country level and he showed last start that he'll run the trip. He's a Maiden taking on BM66 company, but he has enough substance to knock this over. PREFER DIAMONDS (7) is the class improver, dropping out of a Randwick BM72 where she was safely held but tackling a more suitable assignment after being near the top of an open market at Hawkesbury two back. TAVIJEWEL (8) was beaten a nose at Orange last week and has a solid record with Izzy Neale, so he stays in the mix if he carries that sharpness to 2000m. GODWITS (3) can go one better this time.",
